{{also|Duodenum}}
==English==
[[Image:Tractus intestinalis duodenum.svg|thumb|A schematic of the [[gastrointestinal tract]], with the duodenum shown in orange-pink.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|en}} (from the phrase {{m|la|[[duodēnum]] [[digitōrum]]||space of twelve digits}}, in reference to its length), from {{m|la|duodēnī||twelve each}} + {{m|la|digitōrum}}, genitive plural of {{m|la|digitus||finger, toe, [[digit]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/djuːə(ʊ)ˈdiːnəm/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-duodenum.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}, {{audio|En-us-ncalif-duodenum.ogg|Audio (Northern California, US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|duodena|duodenums}}

# The first part of the [[small intestine]], starting at the lower end of the [[stomach]] and extending to the [[jejunum]].

====Derived terms====
* [[duodenal]]
* [[duodenitis]]

====Synonyms====
* [[dodecadactylum]], [[maw-gut]] {{qualifier|both obsolete}}

